{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "דרך הבשן", :translit "derech ha-bashan", :gloss "the way of Bashan"} {:he "שן", :translit "shen", :gloss "tooth"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: בשן read as ב-שן, 'with a tooth' or 'in a tooth'"}], :frame {:text "The Talmud identifies Og king of Bashan as the giant survivor of the Refa'im (Deuteronomy 3:11), and rabbinic tradition elaborates various wonders about his enormous body. The Ba'al HaTurim reads the place-name Bashan (בשן) as containing the word שן ('tooth'), suggesting a tradition — which he attributes to a work called HaRo'eh — that Og possessed a supernaturally large tooth. The reference to HaRo'eh likely points to a specific midrashic or halakhic work known in medieval rabbinic circles.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 3:11" "Niddah 61a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: בשן read as ב-שן, 'with a tooth' or 'in a tooth'", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:33:36.379288546Z", :model "glm-5.2"}